    <briefdescription>
<para>Wave D — Query Engine Dedicated Performance Benchmark Gates. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Four benchmark gates for the query engine hot paths using in-process stubs. Results are captured and compared against the thresholds below during the Wave D sign-off run.</para>
<sect1 id="bench__query__dedicated__gates_8cpp_1autotoc_md10_1s1"><sect2 id="bench__query__dedicated__gates_8cpp_1autotoc_md10">
<title>Gate definitions</title><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>QE-BM-01 : Parse p95 latency ≤ 500 µs per query</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>QE-BM-02 : Plan p95 latency ≤ 2 000 µs per query</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>QE-BM-03 : Execute p95 latency ≤ 5 000 µs per query</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>QE-BM-04 : Concurrent throughput ≥ 2 000 queries/sec (8 threads)</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</sect2></sect1>
